{-| Ficus (generated by ficus-tools/gen_sized.py, do not edit; docs/SIZED-PLAN.md): the signed 16 bit integer `Int16`, -32768 to 32767. Arithmetic wraps around (two's complement, no check, no trap); `//`, `modBy` and `remainderBy` by zero give 0. Literals are checked against the range at compile time.

The operators, comparisons, `Dict` keys and `List.sort` work through the members below (decision A3); the specializer replaces every
member and every function marked (kernel) by the C operation of runtime/fic_sized.h, so the bodies only give the types (`zero` is the
literal 0 at the type, A5c). The module is
added to the source directories of `.c` and `.mono` builds (Ficus.Mono.Overlay); a module `Int16` of the project or of a package of the
same name wins over this one (Build.crawlModule). `Int16(..)` is exported so that the members are visible to the type checker.
-}

